# Codex, and OpenCode signed in with ChatGPT.
allow https://chatgpt.com/     read method=POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE  # model traffic for a ChatGPT plan
allow https://api.openai.com/  read method=POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE  # API-key use
allow https://auth.openai.com/ read method=POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE  # issues the device code and the tokens

# Measured with codex 0.169.0 on 2026-11-13 (doc/agent-measurement.md, "Measurement"):
# - Modes: the interactive TUI, with two turns and two compactions; codex exec with tool calls, codex exec resume and
#   a turn that spawns a subagent. Signed in with ChatGPT, and codex exec also with an API key. codex logout, codex
#   login --device-auth, and a token refresh that a rejected access token forced.
# - The path, refused and error lines are what MeasurementReport accepts (doc/agent-measurement.md, "The
#   measurement suite"). Each <...> stands for one label of a host name.
#   path chatgpt.com /backend-api/codex/responses /backend-api/codex/models /backend-api/codex/analytics-events/events
#   path chatgpt.com /backend-api/wham/accounts/check /backend-api/wham/usage /backend-api/wham/security-setup
#   path chatgpt.com /backend-api/wham/rate-limit-reset-credits /backend-api/wham/settings/user
#   path chatgpt.com /backend-api/ps/plugins/installed /backend-api/ps/plugins/suggested/codex
#   path chatgpt.com /backend-api/ps/plugins/list /backend-api/ps/mcp /backend-api/ps/apps/batch
#   path chatgpt.com /backend-api/codex/alpha/search
#   path api.openai.com /v1/responses
#   path auth.openai.com /oauth/revoke /api/accounts/deviceauth/usercode /api/accounts/deviceauth/token /oauth/token
#   refused chatgpt.com GET /backend-api/codex/responses
#   refused api.openai.com GET /v1/responses
#   refused ab.chatgpt.com CONNECT
#   refused sdmntpr<region>.oaiusercontent.com CONNECT
#   error chatgpt.com relay: client: Broken pipe
# - Under an API key, codex exec also fetches /backend-api/codex/models from chatgpt.com, sending the same key.
# - The device code login polls /api/accounts/deviceauth/token about every five seconds until the user approves.
#   auth.openai.com's codes and tokens travel in bodies, so its lines carry no cred=.
# - Every request body declared a Content-Length. Every request to chatgpt.com and api.openai.com carried a
#   credential, one index per key or token: the refreshed token shows as a new index.
# - The error: `relay: client: Broken pipe` on /backend-api/codex/responses, as a codex exec process exited after its
#   turn completed.
# - The refusals:
#   - the WebSocket upgrade at /backend-api/codex/responses, answered 426: each new codex exec process, codex exec
#     resume and each subagent included, tries once and falls back to HTTPS for its turns. The TUI was measured while
#     the proxy answered 403, when it tried 14 times before its first turn and never again;
#   - the WebSocket upgrade at /v1/responses, answered 403: each new process tries 7 times over about 7 seconds
#     before the same fallback (doc/design.md, "WebSocket only at a path that a line names");
#   - ab.chatgpt.com, below;
#   - sdmntpr<region>.oaiusercontent.com, five CONNECTs at each codex exec start under a ChatGPT sign-in.
# - Other hosts: raw.githubusercontent.com, the TUI's /openai/codex/main/announcement_tip.toml.
# - On 2026-11-14, codex exec as ko-review's reviewer sent /backend-api/codex/alpha/search three times. Codex's
#   standalone web search posts each web.run operation there with the conversation's tail: the previous user message,
#   up to 1,000 tokens of assistant text after it, and the current one (rust-v0.169.0,
#   codex-rs/codex-api/src/endpoint/search.rs and codex-rs/ext/web-search/src/history.rs).

# Measured with opencode 1.19.5 on 2026-11-14, signed in with "ChatGPT Pro/Plus (headless)", on openai/gpt-6-astra,
# under deny-unless-allowed:
# - Modes: opencode run with a shell call and a subagent that makes its own shell call; opencode run --session with a
#   shell call; the TUI in this repository, with two turns, /compact and a message; the sign-in; a turn after a token
#   refresh, forced by moving openai.expires in ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json into the past; the TUI with a turn
#   under deny-unless-model.
# - Every request went to a path that the path lines above list, as opencode/1.19.5: model calls to
#   /backend-api/codex/responses, and the sign-in and the refresh to auth.openai.com. OpenCode tried no WebSocket.
# - Every body declared a Content-Length. Every request to chatgpt.com carried a credential; the refreshed token shows
#   as a new index.
# - The TUI asks registry.npmjs.org for opencode's latest version at each start, and one of its connections sends no
#   byte before closing:
#   error registry.npmjs.org tunnel: expected 5 bytes, got 0
# - At its first start in the volume, opencode installed @opencode-ai/plugin, pinned to its own version, into
#   ~/.config/opencode with its own npm, and the install completed. The defaults' read-only line for the registry
#   refused npm's audit, and one connection ended in the handshake:
#   refused registry.npmjs.org POST /-/npm/v1/security/advisories/bulk
#   error registry.npmjs.org tunnel: Remote host terminated the handshake
# - Under deny-unless-model, opencode was refused at each start at its model catalog's host and at the registry, and
#   the turn completed:
#   refused models.opencode.ai CONNECT
#   refused registry.npmjs.org CONNECT
# - One opencode run, started after the stored expiry moved, sent nothing after its catalog read from
#   models.opencode.ai, and hung until killed after five minutes. The next run refreshed the token and completed.

# ab.chatgpt.com serves A/B configuration and telemetry. The host is absent: codex works without it, and a refusal
# produces a log line.
